adr: 0304
file: selfhost/apfront.pas
kills: generic_infer_partial
why: The husk removal walks formals and actuals in lockstep again, as it could while every activation wrote all of its type arguments or none. An omitted type parameter consumed no actual, so stepping over one for it deletes the value actual that follows and the produced routine is called with the wrong list.
--- old
        if g^.grIsTypeDisc then begin
          j := j + 1;
          { An omitted type parameter consumed no actual, so the walk does not
            step over one for it. }
          if j <= nWritten then begin
            nxt := a^.next;
            if prev = nil then args := nxt else prev^.next := nxt;
            a := nxt
          end
        end
--- new
        if g^.grIsTypeDisc then begin
          nxt := a^.next;
          if prev = nil then args := nxt else prev^.next := nxt;
          a := nxt
        end
